entries.description:
The number of ways of selecting 3 students from a group of 5 students is
\binom{5}{3} = \frac{5!}{3!2!}
= \frac{5 \times 4 \times 3!}{3!2!}
= \frac{5 \times 4}{2}
= 10.

The number of ways of selecting 2 students from a group of 5 students is
\binom{5}{2} = \frac{5!}{2!3!}
= \frac{5 \times 4 \times 3!}{2!3!}
= \frac{5 \times 4}{2}
= 10.
